<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33717" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Păphos</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-us</span></b> ), i, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πάφος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city on the island of Cyprus</i>, <i>sacred to Venus</i>, <i>with a
				celebrated temple of Venus</i>, <i>the modern
				Baffo</i>, <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 1, 30, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 7,
			5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 96, 97, § 210</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 2,
			2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">est celsa mihi Paphos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 10, 51</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illa Paphon veterem linquens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 5, 61</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">qui eum de Pharsalicā fugā
					Paphum persecuti sunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Phil. 2, 15, 39</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Păphĭă-cus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>Paphian</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Avien. Perieg.
			227</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Păphĭē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., <i>the
				Paphian</i>, i. e. <i>Venus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sive cupis Paphien,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					7, 74, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 14,
			21</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A sort of lettuce that grew on the island of
			Cyprus</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 10, 193</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Păphĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Paphian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paphiae myrti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. A.
					A. 3, 181</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paphia Venus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					2, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lampades,</span>”
				<i>the planet Venus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 5, 4, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nicocles,</span>”
				<i>of Paphos</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 37, 63, § 167</span></i>
			.—In plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Păphii</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>the
				inhabitants of Paphos</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				13, 48</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Paphii thyrsi, <i>the stalks of the Cyprian
				lettuce</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 10, 370</span></i>.</div>
